# string-and-unicode

## Installation

You can install this package via npm:

```bash
$ npm install --save string-and-unicode
```

Then, load it into your project:

```javascript
var stringAndUnicode = require('string-and-unicode');
```

Now you can use the exported function:

```javascript
console.log(stringAndUnicode('Hello World')); // ['Hello', 'World']
```
